      "question": "How did Qualcomm's customer-concentration and customer-designed-chip risks change from FY2024 to FY2025? Give me a concise risk brief that distinguishes a stronger warning from a new exposure, then connect the comparison to relevant later developments involving major handset customers. Make clear which effects are reported facts and which remain expectations.",
      "answer": "- **Bottom line: a stronger warning, not a new exposure.** FY2024 already anticipated Apple replacing Qualcomm modems and described Samsung and Chinese customers designing their own chips. FY2025 explicitly names **Apple, Samsung and Xiaomi**, and says increasing Apple modem substitution **“will have a significant negative impact”** on QCT revenue, operating results and cash flow. That is management’s expectation—not a quantified, realized loss established by these risk disclosures. [S5] [S6]\n\n- **Customer concentration remained structurally similar.** Both years warn that reliance on a few premium-handset customers creates purchasing-power, order-timing and customer-loss risks. FY2025 brings the stronger Apple substitution warning directly into this factor and clarifies that the adverse product-mix effect concerns Apple devices using Qualcomm modems. The wording does not establish that customer concentration itself increased. [S3] [S4]\n\n- **Later developments support continued exposure, with limits:**\n  - **Apple:** On July 30, 2026, 9to5Mac reported that some iPhones already used Apple’s cellular chips while most still used Qualcomm modems. Its discussion of broader C2 adoption was explicitly prospective and rumor-based—not confirmation of completed replacement or resulting Qualcomm revenue losses. The excerpt does not establish when the existing deployments began relative to the filing. [W4]\n  - **Xiaomi:** Bloomberg reported on August 24, 2026 that Xiaomi launched its Xring O3 mobile processor. That is a reported post-filing chip announcement consistent with the disclosed vertical-integration risk; it does **not** establish completed handset deployment, displacement volumes or realized Qualcomm revenue losses. [W3]\n  - **Samsung:** The returned evidence did not establish a supported dated post-filing substitution event; that is not evidence that none occurred.\n\n- **Comparison basis:** Original 10-Ks: FY2024, September 25, 2023–September 29, 2024, filed November 6, 2024, accession 0000804328-24-000075; FY2025, September 30, 2024–September 28, 2025, filed November 5, 2025, accession 0000804328-25-000085. Later context was checked from November 6, 2025 through October 22, 2026. [S1] [S2]\n\nUnresolved outputs:\n- The complete request could not be checked; the answer covers the recognized filing tasks only.",
